-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
~doesnotexist arg

-- replay --
$ dorc --book=book.sh --results -
#!/bin/sh
# dorc probe (read-only): checks per-SITE convergence, mutates nothing.
# When run, emits one results-record per site on stdout (the return channel):
#   site <leafid> effect=<holds|absent|cant-tell> rc=<n>
# effect is derived from the probe command's rc (0=holds, 1=absent, else cant-tell);
# rc is the raw PROBE-command status (opaque to Dorc -- the record is the out-of-band lane).

printf 'dorc-records/1 nonce=dorc attempt=1 host=localhost book=998393f5d98d8bc3d129398a0c8b0427af895c135188054bfbfc416f8427265b sites=0 @@dorc@@\n'
# site:0 unresolvable-no-probe
printf 'dorc-records-end/1 nonce=dorc @@dorc@@\n'
classify: note[cmdsub-operand-top]: the command word is an unquoted field-split
/ glob / tilde expansion, so Dorc cannot know its value until the command runs
on the host -- there is nothing to resolve and no read-only probe to check. Dorc
elides a command only when it can prove the command's effect is already in
place, so this one is left to run on every apply.
      [ book.sh:2:1
   2 | ~doesnotexist arg
     | \___________/

   = repair:  Give the operand a value Dorc can resolve statically -- a literal,
              or a variable assigned from one -- so Dorc can probe it and elide
              the command once it has converged. If the value must stay dynamic,
              load an oracle that vouches for this command's convergence, and
              Dorc will guard the command instead of running it every time.
probe: note[site-unresolvable]: sm 1 site run unprobed (no read-only check could
be shipped): `~doesnotexist arg` -- run `dorc why` for the per-site detail (the
apply runs each anyway, to stay safe)
      [ book.sh:2:1
   2 | ~doesnotexist arg
     | \_______________/

   = help:  sm site runs `~doesnotexist arg`
why: ran because the command word is a command-substitution `$(...)` or runtime-dynamic value -- its value couldn't be resolved (first seen at 2:1 `~doesnotexist arg`); so dorc runs it, to stay safe (when unsure, run). to skip it, make the operand a literal Dorc can resolve+probe [resolve-dynamism]
hint: '~doesnotexist' (line 2) is unmodeled: it is the first wall -- an oracle vouching its convergence would elide it when converged
dorc: run `dorc why` for the per-site cause-chains, or `dorc why book.sh:N` to query a source line
#!/bin/sh
# dorc apply: the book, with already-converged/dead lines elided (value-preserving stand-in).

#!/bin/sh
~doesnotexist arg
emission: warning[emitted-line-unsafe-for-paste]: [unwritten:
emitted-line-unsafe-for-paste]
dorc: plan-summary sites=1 elide=0 omit=0 guard=0 run=1 may-alias=0
dorc: decision-digest 8281b2d5cd6a5abe2c6a8a21c058d95c8b80db3a081fb3775be263993052bc4c
